/a></i></td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/mak_13pro'>nɲa</a></i> </td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/mak_3a_rem'>kɨn-/kini-</a></i></td></tr></table><table class="table paradigm-table"><caption>Intransitive person marking</caption><tr><td class="td paradigm-td"> </td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">1</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/mak_1p'>Ø/j-/ɨ-</a></i>, <i><a href='/morpheme/mak_1sa'>w-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">2</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/mak_2p'>ə(j)-/a(j)-/o(j)-</a></i>, <i><a href='/morpheme/mak_2sa'>m-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">1+2</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/mak_12sa'>k(V)-</a></i>, <i><a href='/morpheme/mak_12'>k(ɨ)-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">1+3</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/mak_13pro'>nɲa</a></i> <i><a href='/morpheme/mak_3_rem'>kɨn-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">3</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/mak_3_rem'>kɨn-</a></i></td></tr></table>	\N	45	7	2	1	2021-01-14 10:01:06.714643+00	2021-01-14 10:01:06.714643+00	t	\N
{}	base	mak_imp	imperative	\N	Only Sp verbs take second person prefixes (<a href='/sources/maquiritaricaceres2011'>Cáceres 2011</a>: 130).\n<table class="table paradigm-table"><caption>Transitive person marking</caption><tr><td class="td paradigm-td"> </td><td class="td paradigm-td">1P</td><td class="td paradigm-td">3P</td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/mak_12'>k(ɨ)-</a></i></td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/mak_t'>t(ɨ)-</a></i>, <i><a href='/morpheme/mak_3i'>Ø/i-</a></i></td></tr></table><table class="table paradigm-table"><caption>Intransitive person marking</caption><tr><td class="td paradigm-td"> </td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">2</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/mak_2p'>ə(j)-/a(j)-/o(j)-</a></i></td></tr></table>	\N	46	7	1	1	2021-01-14 10:01:06.714643+00	2021-01-14 10:01:06.714643+00	t	\N
{}	base	ara_int	intermediate past	\N	Person marking is identical to the <a href='/construction/ara_main'>Arara mixed Set I/II clause</a>, except for third person, where <i><a href='/morpheme/ara_3int'>mon(i)-</a></i> is found. Notably, this marker cannot co-occur with the TAM marker <i>-te</i>, which does occur with the other person prefixes (<a href='/sources/alves2017arara'>Alves 2017</a>: 155). Although the description indicates that all third person scenarios are marked with <i>mon(i)-</i>, it seems like Sp verbs do not receive the marker. There is only one example of an Sp verb in the intermediate past with a third person argument, and it shows the idiosyncratic marker <i>ju-</i>:  <blockquote style='margin-top: 5px; margin-bottom: 5px'>     (<a href='/example/ara-43'>1</a>) <a href='/languages/ara'>Arara</a> (<a href='/sources/alves2017arara'>Alves 2017</a>: 85)     <div class="sentence-wrapper"><div class="sentence"><div class="body"><div class="gloss-box"><div class="gloss-unit"><div class="word"><text>ju-bage-lɨ</text></div><div class="gloss">3.Sp-wake.up-REC</div></div><div class="gloss-unit"><div class="word"><text>uraŋmo</text></div><div class="gloss">child</div></div></div><div class="translation">The child woke up.</div></div></div></div> </blockquote> All other examples of intransitive verbs with third person arguments in the intermediate past are with Sa verbs.\n<table class="table paradigm-table"><caption>Transitive person marking</caption><tr><td class="td paradigm-td"> </td><td class="td paradigm-td">1P</td><td class="td paradigm-td">2P</td><td class="td paradigm-td">1+2P</td><td class="td paradigm-td">1+3P</td><td class="td paradigm-td">3P</td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">1A</td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_1on2'>k(o)(w)-</a></i></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_1a'>j-/in(i)-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">2A</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_12'>ugu-</a></i></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td">? </td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_2a'>m(i)-</a></i>, <i><a href='/morpheme/ara_2sa'>m(ɨ)-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">1+2A</td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_12a'>kud-/kut-/kut͡ʃi-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">1+3A</td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td">? </td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td">? </td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">3A</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_1p'>j-/ɨ(w)-</a></i></td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_2p'>o(w)-</a></i></td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_12'>ugu-</a></i></td><td class="td paradigm-td">? </td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_3int'>mon(i)-</a></i></td></tr></table><table class="table paradigm-table"><caption>Intransitive person marking</caption><tr><td class="td paradigm-td"> </td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">1</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_1p'>j-/ɨ(w)-</a></i>, <i><a href='/morpheme/ara_1sa'>w(ɨ)-</a></i>, <i><a href='/morpheme/ara_1sa1'>k-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">2</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_2p'>o(w)-</a></i>, <i><a href='/morpheme/ara_2sa'>m(ɨ)-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">1+2</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_12'>ugu-</a></i>, <i><a href='/morpheme/ara_12sa'>kut-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">1+3</td><td class="td paradigm-td">? </td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">3</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_3i'>Ø/i-</a></i>, <i><a href='/morpheme/ara_3int'>mon(i)-</a></i></td></tr></table>	\N	49	13	2	1	2021-01-14 10:01:06.714643+00	2021-01-14 10:01:06.714643+00	t	\N
{}	base	ara_rem	remote past	\N	Person marking is identical to the <a href='/construction/ara_main'>Arara mixed Set I/II clause</a>, except for third person, where <i><a href='/morpheme/ara_3rem'>kun(i)-</a></i> is found. Notably, this marker cannot co-occur with the TAM marker <i>-ne</i>, which does occur with the other person prefixes (<a href='/sources/alves2017arara'>Alves 2017</a>: 154). There are no examples of Sp verbs in the remote past, and, similarly to the <a href='/construction/ara_int'>Arara intermediate past clause</a>, it is unclear whether they would take <i><a href='/morpheme/ara_3rem'>kun(i)-</a></i> or the Sp marker <i><a href='/morpheme/ara_3i'>Ø/i-</a></i>.\n<table class="table paradigm-table"><caption>Transitive person marking</caption><tr><td class="td paradigm-td"> </td><td class="td paradigm-td">1P</td><td class="td paradigm-td">2P</td><td class="td paradigm-td">1+2P</td><td class="td paradigm-td">1+3P</td><td class="td paradigm-td">3P</td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">1A</td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_1on2'>k(o)(w)-</a></i></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_1a'>j-/in(i)-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">2A</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_12'>ugu-</a></i></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td">? </td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_2a'>m(i)-</a></i>, <i><a href='/morpheme/ara_2sa'>m(ɨ)-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">1+2A</td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/ara_12a'>kud-/kut-/kut͡ʃi-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">1+3A</td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td">? </td><td class="td pa