{}	base	pem_old	inherited	\N	This is what remains of the Set I construction. As in other Pemongan languages, it is functionally restricted, in <a href='/languages/pem'>Pemón</a> it prominently occurs in questions (and answers to these questions). Local and inverse scenarios rarely occur, mostly direct and third person scenarios are found. Forms with <i><a href='/cognateset/12'>*k-</a></i> now have a prohibitive meaning, as in <a href='/languages/mac'>Macushi</a>. I have not found any examples for 2>1 scenarios. 1S is zero-marked (remnants of <i>*u-</i> are present), so one would expect 2>1 to be, too.\n<table class="table paradigm-table"><caption>Transitive person marking</caption><tr><td class="td paradigm-td"> </td><td class="td paradigm-td">2P</td><td class="td paradigm-td">3P</td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">1A</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/pem_2p'>a(j)-</a></i></td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/pem_1a'>s(V)-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">2A</td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/pem_2s'>m(V)-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">3A</td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/pem_3n'>n(V)-</a></i></td></tr></table><table class="table paradigm-table"><caption>Intransitive person marking</caption><tr><td class="td paradigm-td"> </td><td class="td paradigm-td"></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">1</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/pem_1s_new'>Ø/u-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">2</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/pem_2s'>m(V)-</a></i></td></tr><tr><td class="td paradigm-td">3</td><td class="td paradigm-td"><i><a href='/morpheme/pem_3n'>n(V)-</a></i></td></tr></table>	\N	53	14	2	1	2021-01-14 10:01:06.714643+00	2021-01-14 10:01:06.714643+00	t	\N
